                                                "sense_id": "d0775f96-cf8e-31ea-9320-2c7bc600a0a1",
                                                "text": "The Club became like town meetings for the entire New York art scene, attracting dealers, collectors, uptown curators like Alfred Barr, critics, and just about any other culturati who could wrangle their way in."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "428bcbf4-7955-45e6-a13c-02f0bd69d338",
